best piece of advice that my therapist  taught me that i now share with my  clients as a therapist to improve any  relationship here it is whatever the  conversation is and whoever it is with i  want you to make sure that you are  actively listening instead of just  waiting for your turn to talk so many  times we get so excited that we just  want to say what we have to say without  even listening to that other person  especially if it's a debate or an  argument and we think we're right and we  just want to aggressively go in there  and say our point but that is not  healthy and not what we want to do what  we want to do is engage in active  listening which is listening with the  intent to understand the way the other  person is feeling this will help us  develop empathy towards that person even  if we don't agree with them empathetic  active listening is proven to help  improve healthy communication and to  help lead to a quicker solution so the  next time you're in a conversation with  somebody i want you to ask am i actively  listening or am i just waiting for my  turn to speak if you're just waiting try  to understand how that person's feeling
 

